<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brimstone Hill Fortress</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brimstone Hill Fortress is a British fortress on a steep volcanic hill on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a>, built mainly between 1690 and 1790 by enslaved African labourers. Known as the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a>', it fell to a French siege in 1782 but was returned under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a> in 1783. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brimstone-hill-fortress.jpg" alt="Brimstone Hill Fortress" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ukexpat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BrimstoneHill01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
